{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"g_legend","type":"group","x":-200,"y":-1950,"width":2800,"height":300,"color":"#8E24AA","label":"COLOR CODING LEGEND & CURRENT STATUS"},
		{"id":"legend_text","type":"text","text":"# Biometric Attendance System — Hardware Integration Canvas\n**Current State (2026-10-01):** ESP32 serial communication **VERIFIED (COM3 @ 115200 baud)** · PlatformIO build **VERIFIED** · R307S fingerprint sensor **ACQUIRED, NOT YET CONNECTED OR POWERED**.\n\n**Visual Color Code Scheme:**\n- 🟩 **GREEN (#50C878):** Verified / Working (COM3 serial, toolchain, SQLite schema, API slice)\n- 🟨 **YELLOW (#FFD000):** Needs Verification (R307S pinout, supply voltage, UART levels, harness mapping)\n- 🟦 **BLUE (#4A90E2):** Planned (10-Phase bring-up, driver abstraction, dashboard, offline queue)\n- 🟥 **RED (#E53935):** Warning / Electrical Risk (5V overvoltage hazard, wire color assumption trap, CR2032 charging hazard)\n- 🟪 **PURPLE (#8E24AA):** Documentation / Reference (Integration plan, wiring, pinout, test gates, handoff)","x":-160,"y":-1900,"width":2720,"height":220,"color":"#8E24AA"},

		{"id":"g_warnings","type":"group","x":-200,"y":-1600,"width":1350,"height":480,"color":"#E53935","label":"CRITICAL HARDWARE & ELECTRICAL WARNINGS (RED)"},
		{"id":"warn_5v","type":"text","text":"### ⚠️ ELECTRICAL HAZARD: 3.3V GPIO LIMIT\nESP32 GPIO pins are **NOT 5V tolerant**.\nConnecting 5V logic to GPIO 16 (RX) will destroy the silicon.\n**MANDATORY:** Measure R307S TX open-circuit voltage with multimeter before connecting. If > 3.3V, use level shifter.","x":-160,"y":-1540,"width":620,"height":200,"color":"#E53935"},
		{"id":"warn_colors","type":"text","text":"### ⚠️ WIRE COLOR ASSUMPTION TRAP\nObserved harness: 1:Red, 2:Black, 3:Yellow, 4:Green, 5:Blue, 6:White.\n**DO NOT ASSUME WIRE COLORS PROVE PINOUT.**\nMany low-cost harnesses insert ribbon cables in arbitrary or reversed order. Always verify ground continuity and silkscreen labels.","x":490,"y":-1540,"width":620,"height":200,"color":"#E53935"},
		{"id":"warn_battery","type":"text","text":"### ⚠️ RTC CHARGING CIRCUIT WARNING\nDS3231 breakout boards often feature a trickle charging diode designed for rechargeable LIR2032 cells. If using a primary (non-rechargeable) CR2032, power the breakout strictly at 3.3V or disable the diode to prevent cell swelling.","x":-160,"y":-1310,"width":1270,"height":150,"color":"#E53935"},

		{"id":"g_unverified","type":"group","x":1220,"y":-1600,"width":1380,"height":480,"color":"#FFD000","label":"R307S HARDWARE TARGET — UNVERIFIED SPECIFICATIONS (YELLOW)"},
		{"id":"r307s_module","type":"text","text":"### 🟡 R307S Optical Fingerprint Sensor\n- **Physical Status:** In hand, 6-wire ribbon harness attached.\n- **Electrical Status:** **NOT YET CONNECTED OR POWERED**.\n- **Sensor Engine:** Optical CMOS prism, onboard DSP.\n- **Resolution / Capacity:** 500 DPI / 1000 templates (typical).\n- **Immediate Next Step:** Physical bench inspection (Phase 1).","x":1260,"y":-1540,"width":640,"height":200,"color":"#FFD000"},
		{"id":"r307s_pins","type":"text","text":"### 🟡 Harness Wire Order (Observed)\n- **Pos 1:** Red (Candidate: VCC 4.2V-6V or 3.3V)\n- **Pos 2:** Black (Candidate: GND)\n- **Pos 3:** Yellow (Candidate: TXD out)\n- **Pos 4:** Green (Candidate: RXD in)\n- **Pos 5:** Blue (Candidate: Touch / Wake)\n- **Pos 6:** White (Candidate: 3.3V / NC)\n*All assignments TO VERIFY via multimeter/silkscreen.*","x":1930,"y":-1540,"width":630,"height":200,"color":"#FFD000"},
		{"id":"r307s_uart_spec","type":"text","text":"### 🟡 UART & Power Requirements (TO VERIFY)\n- Supply Voltage: Confirm if 5V rail (VIN) or 3.3V direct.\n- TX Logic Level: Measure open-circuit voltage relative to GND (must be <= 3.3V).\n- Default Baud Rate: 57600 baud (provisional default; test ladder if needed).","x":1260,"y":-1310,"width":1300,"height":150,"color":"#FFD000"},

		{"id":"g_verified","type":"group","x":-200,"y":-1070,"width":1350,"height":550,"color":"#50C878","label":"VERIFIED SUBSYSTEMS & WORKING EVIDENCE (GREEN)"},
		{"id":"esp32_verified","type":"text","text":"### 🟢 ESP32 Microcontroller (Phase 0 PASSED)\n- **Hardware:** ESP32-WROOM-32 DevKit V1.\n- **Port:** Confirmed working on **COM3** at 115200 baud.\n- **Status:** Baseline toolchain test sketch compiled, flashed to hardware, and verified via USB serial output.\n- **Heap & Chip ID:** Reported cleanly in boot telemetry.","x":-160,"y":-1010,"width":620,"height":220,"color":"#50C878"},
		{"id":"pio_build_verified","type":"file","file":"firmware/platformio.ini","x":490,"y":-1010,"width":620,"height":220,"color":"#50C878"},
		{"id":"db_verified","type":"file","file":"backend/migrations/001_initial_schema.sql","x":-160,"y":-760,"width":620,"height":210,"color":"#50C878"},
		{"id":"api_verified","type":"file","file":"backend/tests/test_api.py","x":490,"y":-760,"width":620,"height":210,"color":"#50C878"},

		{"id":"g_planned","type":"group","x":1220,"y":-1070,"width":1380,"height":550,"color":"#4A90E2","label":"PLANNED R307S INTEGRATION & PHASES (BLUE)"},
		{"id":"phases_node","type":"text","text":"### 🔵 10-Phase Bring-Up Sequence\n- **Phase 0:** ESP32 serial test (PASSED - COM3 @ 115200)\n- **Phase 1:** Verify documentation & physical pinout (NEXT)\n- **Phase 2:** Connect minimum wiring (GND, VCC, TX, RX)\n- **Phase 3:** Power-on sanity test (voltages & thermals)\n- **Phase 4:** Establish UART communication (UART2 @ 57600)\n- **Phase 5:** Minimal command & response (ACK 0x00)\n- **Phase 6:** Read system parameters (capacity = 1000)\n- **Phase 7:** Test 2-pass fingerprint enrollment\n- **Phase 8:** Test 1:N fingerprint matching\n- **Phase 9:** Attendance pipeline integration","x":1260,"y":-1010,"width":640,"height":460,"color":"#4A90E2"},
		{"id":"hal_node","type":"file","file":"firmware/include/fingerprint_sensor.h","x":1930,"y":-1010,"width":630,"height":220,"color":"#4A90E2"},
		{"id":"config_h_node","type":"file","file":"firmware/include/config.h","x":1930,"y":-760,"width":630,"height":210,"color":"#4A90E2"},

		{"id":"g_reference","type":"group","x":-200,"y":-470,"width":2800,"height":480,"color":"#8E24AA","label":"DOCUMENTATION, PINOUTS & REFERENCE GUIDES (PURPLE)"},
